- No, this is not good.

05:47.347 --> 05:50.115
I think we somehow sent
ourselves into a cutaway.

05:50.116 --> 05:51.750
So, what's the special occasion?

05:51.751 --> 05:53.820
I'm marrying my catamaran.

05:57.791 --> 05:59.592
I don't understand how we got here.

05:59.593 --> 06:01.460
All I know is that we both set up

06:01.461 --> 06:03.062
this cutaway at the same time,

06:03.063 --> 06:05.731
and now we're inside
this cutaway in Australia.

06:05.732 --> 06:07.700
That'll be 23 Australian dollars,

06:07.701 --> 06:09.535
- not regular dollars.
- See?

06:09.536 --> 06:12.605
So, you and I set up a cutaway
at the same time

06:12.606 --> 06:15.708
and that somehow put us <i>in</i> the cutaway?

06:15.709 --> 06:17.610
Well, this is weirder
than an uptight guy

06:17.611 --> 06:19.479
at an Eagles concert.

06:20.447 --> 06:21.714
(CHEERING)

06:21.715 --> 06:24.817
Who out there wants to...
"Take It Easy"?

06:24.818 --> 06:27.152
Not me. Do you read the papers?

06:27.153 --> 06:28.320
Look around you.

06:28.321 --> 06:30.422
All right. Well, you want to...

06:30.423 --> 06:32.825
- "Take It to the Limit"?
- Not really.

06:32.826 --> 06:35.261
That would be
a little foolhardy, wouldn't it?

06:35.262 --> 06:36.629
Okay. This time,

06:36.630 --> 06:39.565
I set up the cutaway by myself,
and it sent us here.

06:39.566 --> 06:42.501
Weird. It's like
this is a whole CutawayLand.

06:42.502 --> 06:44.570
And it takes a setup from both of us

06:44.571 --> 06:46.739
to get us in or out of CutawayLand

06:46.740 --> 06:49.842
but only one of us
to move <i>within</i> CutawayLand.

06:49.843 --> 06:52.745
Lois, are you saying that it
takes a setup from both of us

06:52.746 --> 06:54.613
to get in or out of CutawayLand

06:54.614 --> 06:57.216
but only one of us
to move within CutawayLand?

06:57.217 --> 07:00.119
Exactly, Peter.
It takes a setup from both of us

07:00.120 --> 07:02.121
to get in or out of CutawayLand

07:02.122 --> 07:04.823
but only one of us
to move within CutawayLand.

07:04.824 --> 07:06.258
I want to be done with this part.

07:06.259 --> 07:09.094
HENLEY: Who likes
"Life in the Fast Lane"?

07:09.095 --> 07:12.097
UPTIGHT GUY: Not anyone
who wants to get there in one piece.

07:12.098 --> 07:13.565
Peter, this may sound crazy,

07:13.566 --> 07:15.501
but this is our chance at the getaway

07:15.502 --> 07:17.169
we didn't have at the beach.

07:17.170 --> 07:18.331
Hey, you're right.

07:18.332 --> 07:20.005
No kids... just you and me.

07:20.006 --> 07:21.473
And we can go anywhere.

07:21.474 --> 07:23.876
Like... like when we
hid in Tom Brady's locker

07:23.877 --> 07:25.645
and watched him shower.

07:29.149 --> 07:30.382
Look at that.

07:30.383 --> 07:32.384
It's just as big as you want it to be

07:32.385 --> 07:34.620
but not so big
that it's gonna distract him.

07:34.621 --> 07:36.388
There's a Trump hat in here.

07:36.389 --> 07:38.157
Don't look at the Trump hat.
Look at his penis.

07:38.158 --> 07:40.125
All right, fine. You ruined this.

07:40.126 --> 07:43.630
This is more frustrating
than Charlton Heston's funeral.

07:46.399 --> 07:47.566
Um, 'scuse me,

07:47.567 --> 07:49.835
is-is this his cold, dead hand?

07:49.836 --> 07:52.404
Uh... yes.

07:52.405 --> 07:54.407
(GRUNTING)

07:55.909 --> 07:58.177
He, uh... he said I could take this.

07:58.178 --> 07:59.378
Oh, oh, I want to do one.

07:59.379 --> 08:01.313
This is better than a spin class

08:01.314 --> 08:05.985
