What's the problem here?

12:31.517 --> 12:34.419
(SCOFFS) They may suck,
but they're our children.

12:34.420 --> 12:37.522
- Tom Devanney?
- Tom Devanney, who in fact has AIDS,

12:37.523 --> 12:39.625
- is next door.
- My mistake.

12:39.626 --> 12:42.928
"Judy Garland Showtime Pills"?

12:42.929 --> 12:44.230
What do these do?

12:45.465 --> 12:48.033
♪ <i>Forget your troubles,</i>
<i>come on, get happy</i> ♪

12:48.034 --> 12:50.402
♪ <i>You better chase</i>
<i>all your cares away.</i> ♪

12:50.403 --> 12:53.372
Peter, enough. I know
you want to have fun with drugs,

12:53.373 --> 12:54.973
but what's the point of drugs

12:54.974 --> 12:56.975
if you don't have kids
to share 'em with?

12:56.976 --> 12:58.777
Damn it, Lois.
We're having fun for once,

12:58.778 --> 13:00.479
but all you can talk about is the kids.

13:00.480 --> 13:03.282
Well, I'm sorry, Peter.
I want to go back.

13:03.283 --> 13:06.985
And with any luck,
we'll get home by wine o'clock.

13:06.986 --> 13:10.489
- What was that?
- Hilarious mom wine joke.

13:10.490 --> 13:14.226
- You think so?
- Oh, I don't think. I <i>pinot.</i>

13:14.227 --> 13:16.461
(LAUGHS) Oh, boy, here I go.

13:16.462 --> 13:18.997
Forgive me, Father, for I have <i>zinned.</i>

13:18.998 --> 13:22.501
- Please-please stop.
- Okay, you don't like these jokes,

13:22.502 --> 13:23.935
but let's see what all the moms

13:23.936 --> 13:26.238
eating soup at Panera Bread think.

13:26.239 --> 13:28.274
(CHEERING)

13:29.475 --> 13:30.909
Well, I don't care if you miss the kids.

13:30.910 --> 13:32.444
I am not gonna let you ruin this.

13:32.445 --> 13:34.946
- Tom Brady's locker.
- Peter, we've already...

13:34.947 --> 13:36.249
Tom Brady's locker.

13:37.650 --> 13:39.318
Okay, Peter, that's it.

13:39.319 --> 13:41.353
We're going home,
and we're going home now.

13:41.354 --> 13:42.754
(SIGHS) All right, fine.

13:42.755 --> 13:44.656
Let's say it at the same time.

13:44.657 --> 13:48.328
This is like the time we were
together with our family.

13:49.662 --> 13:51.730
Wh-Where am I?

13:51.731 --> 13:53.365
Mom? Dad?

13:53.366 --> 13:56.034
I haven't been given a morsel
of food since you left,

13:56.035 --> 13:57.936
by the way. Not one (BLEEP) crumb.

13:57.937 --> 14:00.072
I was just driving a car a second ago.

14:00.073 --> 14:01.708
That's a problem, right?

14:05.111 --> 14:08.280
And now to exhibit the only
power I have in this world.

14:08.281 --> 14:09.614
Stop.

14:09.615 --> 14:11.450
Hey, stop.

14:11.451 --> 14:13.018
He's not stopping.

14:13.019 --> 14:15.187
You're supposed to stop for my hand.

14:15.188 --> 14:17.689
You're supposed to stop for my hand!

14:17.690 --> 14:21.059
You're supposed to stop for my hand!

14:21.060 --> 14:23.462
You're supposed to stop

14:23.463 --> 14:26.631
for my hand!

14:26.632 --> 14:29.201
- What is this?
- It's just a little mix-up.

14:29.202 --> 14:30.669
Peter, let's try it again.

14:30.670 --> 14:32.704
This is like the time we were together

14:32.705 --> 14:34.974
with our family <i>at home.</i>

14:36.476 --> 14:38.276
What... Why didn't it work?

14:38.277 --> 14:41.279
This is better than being at home.

14:41.280 --> 14:44.783
"We make a better team than" at home.

14:44.784 --> 14:46.418
"Worse than" at home?

14:46.419 --> 14:48.353
"The AIDS person is Tom Devanney,

14:48.354 --> 14:51.524
which is the name
of a <i>Family Guy</i> writer" home?

14:54.293 --> 14:57.929
Oh, God, Peter.
I think we're stuck here.

14:57.930 --> 15:00.232
Yeah. I'm also bummed 'cause I'm missing

15:00.233 --> 15:03.001
that Australian guy's marriage
to his catamaran.

15:03.002 --> 15:05.670
Didgeridoo you take this boat
to be your wife?

15:05.671 --> 15:07.239
- I didgeridoo.
- And now,

15:07.240 --> 15:09.107
if there are any spiders
the size of dinner plates

15:09.108 --> 15:10.442
that object to this marriage,

15:10.443 --> 15:13.078
please speak now
or forever hold your peace.

15:13.079 --> 15:14.646
Go get 'em, mate!

15:14.647 --> 15:17.182
I now pronounce you man and boat.

15:17.183 --> 15:18.850
("WEDDING MARCH" PLAYING ON DIDGERIDOO)

15:18.851 --> 15:20.920
(CHEERING)

15:26.492 --> 15:28.093
Wait, so, when you two disappeared,

15:28.094 --> 15:29.895
you were just doing cutaways?

15:29.896 --> 15:32.664
- And now we're all trapped here?
- In our defense,

15:32.665 --> 15:34.433
we only disappeared
'cause we don't like you.

15:34.434 --> 15:36.935
How did we get here? What is this place?

15:36.936 --> 15:39.004
Well, Chris, it's CutawayLand.

15:39.005 --> 15:40.639
Well, what are the rules here?

15:40.640 --> 15:43.742
(SIGHS) Okay. It takes a setup
from both of us.

15:43.743 --> 15:46.144
♪ <i>Highway</i> ♪

15:46.145 --> 15:48.847
♪ <i>Let me slip away on you</i> ♪

15:48.848 --> 15:51.550
♪ <i>Carefree highway</i> ♪

15:51.551 --> 15:54.219
♪ <i>You seen better days.</i> ♪

15:54.220 --> 15:55.687
And that's how it works.

15:55.688 --> 15:57.956
I still don't fully understand.

15:57.957 --> 15:59.391
(SIGHS) Okay.

15:59.392 --> 16:01.993
In order to move within CutawayLand...

16:01.994 --> 16:04.696
♪ <i>An old-time movie</i> ♪

16:04.697 --> 16:08.700
♪ <i>'Bout a ghost from a wishing well</i> ♪

16:08.701 --> 16:11.937
♪ <i>In a castle dark.</i> ♪

16:11.938 --> 16:14.539
I still don't get it,
but let's just move on.

16:14.540 --> 16:16.174
What are we gonna do, Mom?

16:16.175 --> 16:18.677
Shut up, everyone, shut up!
First things first,

16:18.678 --> 16:20.879
did you clean up the house
before coming to CutawayLand?

16:20.880 --> 16:24.149
'Cause if it's found messy,
it's gonna reflect poorly on me.

16:24.150 --> 16:26.318
Hello? Anyone?

16:26.319 --> 16:27.719
Hmm, quite messy.

16:27.720 --> 16:29.387
That reflects poorly on Mrs. Griffin.

16:29.388 --> 16:31.156
Sorry to intrude.

16:31.157 --> 16:34.226
I just wanted to let myself in
to your private residence.

16:34.227 --> 16:36.595
Huh. Nobody's home.

16:36.596 --> 16:38.463
Nobody's home?

16:38.464 --> 16:40.499
Principal party!

16:40.500 --> 16:41.967
("MANNISH BOY" BY MUDDY WATERS PLAYING)

16:41.968 --> 16:43.503
♪ <i>Now, when I was a young boy</i> ♪

16:45.671 --> 16:47.673
♪ <i>At the age of five</i> ♪

16:49.208 --> 16:51.143
♪ <i>My mother said I was gonna be</i> ♪

16:52.645 --> 16:54.480
♪ <i>The greatest man alive</i> ♪

16:56.048 --> 16:58.084
♪ <i>But now I'm a man</i> ♪

16:59.485 --> 17:01.053
♪ <i>Way past 21.</i> ♪

17:02.755 --> 17:05.857
We got to get out of here.
Come on, let's think.

17:05.858 --> 17:07.425
Huh, look at that.

17:07.426 --> 17:10.161
They've got every other team's
playbook alphabetized.

17:10.162 --> 17:12.297
Don't look at the Patriots'
rampant cheating.

17:12.298 --> 17:13.532
Look at the Trump hat.

17:13.533 --> 17:14.933
There's a phone.

17:14.934 --> 17:16.768
Maybe we can call someone for help.

17:16.769 --> 17:19.371
Joe was looking for you guys
before. Maybe he can help.

17:19.372 --> 17:20.873
I'll give it a try.

17:21.841 --> 17:23.909
This cord is all tangled up.

17:23.910 --> 17:26.077
What do I do,
Patriots owner Robert Kraft?

17:26.078 --> 17:29.114
Just give it a tug.
It'll straighten out.

17:29.115 --> 17:30.850
(AIR HORN BLOWS)

17:32.351 --> 17:35.186
All right, I'm calling Joe.

17:35.187 --> 17:36.821
(LINE RINGS)

17:36.822 --> 17:41.493
<i>JOE (ON RECORDING): ♪ Joe
is on a vacation far away</i> ♪

17:41.494 --> 17:43.461
♪ <i>You called him up to talk it over</i> ♪

17:43.462 --> 17:45.096
(SIGHS) Oh, yeah, this thing.

17:45.097 --> 17:48.433
♪ <i>So many things that you want to say</i> ♪

17:48.434 --> 17:52.370
♪ <i>Leave your message</i>
<i>when the beep is over</i> ♪

17:52.371 --> 17:56.341
♪ <i>I don't wanna miss your call tonight</i> ♪

17:56.342 --> 18:00.011
Super long.

18:00.012 --> 18:03.748
♪ <i>I already missed your call tonight</i> ♪

18:03.749 --> 18:05.750
- (BEEP)
- Joe, pick up.

18:05.751 --> 18:07.452
Pick up, Joe.

18:07.453 --> 18:10.288
Hey, Joe, what's with
these crooks on Wall Street?

18:10.289 --> 18:12.824
Oh, my God, don't even get me
started on those guys.

18:12.825 --> 18:14.759
Joe, shut up. No one cares.
Just tell me,

18:14.760 --> 18:16.895
are you in the real world,
or are you a cutaway?

18:16.896 --> 18:18.597
Uh, no, I'm at home.

18:18.598 --> 18:21.032
- Why, do you need me for a cutaway?
- Okay, good.

18:21.033 --> 18:22.968
Just making sure you're not Cutaway Joe.

18:22.969 --> 18:24.869
Hey, you know, that should be
your answering machine.

18:24.870 --> 18:27.672
Cutaway Joe to "Cotton Eye Joe."

18:27.673 --> 18:29.341
Call me back in three minutes.

18:29.342 --> 18:31.811
- Joe, we don't have...
- Call me back in three minutes.

18:34.246 --> 18:36.047
<i>JOE (ON RECORDING): ♪ I just called you,
where did you go?</i> ♪

18:36.048 --> 18:38.516
♪ <i>Where did you run to, Cutaway Joe?</i> ♪

18:38.517 --> 18:40.885
- Hilarious, right?
- Joe, we're stuck in CutawayLand.

18:40.886 --> 18:42.587
- How do we get out?
- Well,

18:42.588 --> 18:45.590
according to a 16-year-old
autistic fan in Akron, Ohio,

18:45.591 --> 18:47.225
"In order for the Griffins to escape

18:47.226 --> 18:49.594
"from a theoretical CutawayLand,
they must first journey

18:49.595 --> 18:51.763
"back to the original <i>Family Guy</i> cutaway

18:51.764 --> 18:53.832
with Adolf Hitler and kill him."

18:53.833 --> 18:55.700
That's it! We'll kill Hitler

18:55.701 --> 18:58.436
to prevent CutawayLand and nothing else.

18:58.437 --> 19:01.139
But how do we get there?
Our setups aren't working.

19:01.140 --> 19:03.074
Well, this is where it gets
a little complicated.

19:03.075 --> 19:05.877
"In order to return
to the original cutaway,

19:05.878 --> 19:08.146
each family member must..."

19:08.147 --> 19:12.283
♪ <i>Does anyone know</i>
<i>where the love of God goes</i> ♪

19:12.284 --> 19:16.288
♪ <i>When the waves</i>
<i>turn the minutes to hours?</i> ♪

19:21.994 --> 19:24.030
(PEOPLE LAUGHING)

19:25.831 --> 19:27.400
(GROWLS)

19:29.368 --> 19:31.436
Wow, Joe's instructions were perfect.

19:31.437 --> 19:33.505
Well, who's going to kill Hitler?

19:33.506 --> 19:36.141
Peter, I got to admit, I'm
not comfortable with this plan.

19:36.142 --> 19:39.077
Yeah, I know he was evil,
but do we really have the right

19:39.078 --> 19:41.246
to take the life of another human being?

19:41.247 --> 19:43.348
Human being? It's Hitler.

19:43.349 --> 19:47.185
Wow, the middle-class morality
of Brian Griffin.

19:47.186 --> 19:48.620
Hitler head, yo!

19:48.621 --> 19:51.823
He cried like a bitch when I did it.

19:51.824 --> 19:53.459
Let's get out of here.

19:55.494 --> 19:57.429
We're... we're back.

19:57.430 --> 19:59.330
Meg, you saved us.

19:59.331 --> 20:01.499
Why are all these principals
in our house?

20:01.500 --> 20:04.536
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

20:04.537 --> 20:06.838
You don't want all these nuts
roaming the streets.

20:06.839 --> 20:09.240
Gary, another LaCroix over here.

20:09.241 --> 20:11.610
- GARY: Pamplemousse?
- If they have it, yeah.

20:14.246 --> 20:16.815
Peter? Peter, are you okay?

20:16.816 --> 20:18.616
Wh-What? What's happening?

20:18.617 --> 20:20.985
You've been passed out for 22 minutes,

20:20.986 --> 20:23.688
babbling about cutaways and Hitler.

20:23.689 --> 20:26.357
- We were so worried.
- I wasn't that worried.

20:26.358 --> 20:28.827
Maybe you shouldn't have eaten
those raw oysters.

20:28.828 --> 20:31.396
I-I'm fine, I'm fine.
Let's just go home.

20:31.397 --> 20:34.232
All right. Let me take this
sweet, sticky Popsicle paper

20:34.233 --> 20:37.236
to that beach trash can
that has bees on it now.

20:42.408 --> 20:44.410
(BUZZING IN DISTANCE)

20:49.415 --> 20:51.483
- Damn it!
- (BEES BUZZING)

20:51.484 --> 20:53.152
(WIND BLOWING)